{"id":"mahabharata-10-004","work":"mahabharata","part":10,"partName":"सौप्तिकपर्व","partNameEn":"Sauptika Parva","unit":4,"title":"चतुर्थोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 4 · Kripa accepts and asks him to wait till morning","summary":{"en":"Kripa, seeing Ashvatthaman's resolve, says he and Kritavarman will follow him, but begs him to rest till morning and then fight with arms. Ashvatthaman refuses to wait, remembering his father's death.","kn":"ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮನ ದೃಢನಿರ್ಧಾರ ಕಂಡ ಕೃಪ ತಾನೂ ಕೃತವರ್ಮನೂ ಅನುಸರಿಸುವುದಾಗಿ ಹೇಳಿ ಬೆಳಗಿನವರೆಗೆ ವಿಶ್ರಮಿಸಿ ಆಯುಧದಿಂದ ಹೋರಾಡಲು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ತಂದೆಯ ಸಾವು ನೆನೆದು ಅಶ್ವತ್ಥಾಮ ಕಾಯಲು ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अश्वत्थामा का संकल्प देखकर कृप कहते हैं कि वे और कृतवर्मा साथ चलेंगे, पर प्रातः तक विश्राम कर शस्त्रों से लड़ने की विनती करते हैं। पिता की मृत्यु याद कर अश्वत्थामा प्रतीक्षा से मना करता है।","te":"అశ్వత్థామ నిశ్చయం చూసి కృపుడు తాను, కృతవర్మ అనుసరిస్తామని చెప్పి ఉదయం వరకు విశ్రమించి ఆయుధాలతో పోరాడమని కోరతాడు. తండ్రి మరణాన్ని గుర్తు చేసుకుని అశ్వత్థామ వేచి ఉండటానికి నిరాకరిస్తాడు.","ta":"அஸ்வத்தாமனின் உறுதியைக் கண்ட கிருபர் தானும் கிருதவர்மனும் தொடர்வதாகக் கூறி, காலை வரை ஓய்வெடுத்து ஆயுதத்துடன் போரிடக் கேட்கிறார். தந்தையின் மரணத்தை நினைத்து அஸ்வத்தாமன் காத்திருக்க மறுக்கிறான்.","ml":"അശ്വത്ഥാമാവിന്റെ നിശ്ചയം കണ്ട കൃപർ, താനും കൃതവർമ്മാവും അദ്ദേഹത്തെ അനുഗമിക്കാമെന്ന് പറയുന്നു; എന്നാൽ പ്രഭാതംവരെ വിശ്രമിച്ച് പിന്നീട് ആയുധങ്ങളുമായി പൊരുതാൻ അപേക്ഷിക്കുന്നു. പിതാവിന്റെ മരണം ഓർത്ത് അശ്വത്ഥാമാവ് കാത്തിരിക്കാൻ വിസമ്മതിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 10.4; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Fri Oct 30 2026","sections":[{"title":"सौप्तिकपर्व","titleEn":"Sauptika Parva (The night massacre)","verses":[{"text":"कृप उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Kripa said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दिष्ट्या ते प्रतिकर्तव्ये मतिर्जातेयमच्युत ।\nन त्वा वारयितुं शक्तो वज्रपाणिरपि स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Faultless one, it is fortunate that your mind has turned to taking vengeance; not even Indra himself, thunderbolt in hand, could hold you back."}},{"n":2,"text":"अनुयास्यावहे त्वां तु प्रभाते सहितावुभौ ।\nअद्य रात्रौ विश्रमस्व विमुक्तकवचध्वजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"We two will follow you together at dawn; for tonight, rest, with armor and banner laid aside."}},{"n":3,"text":"अहं त्वामनुयास्यामि कृतवर्मा च सात्वतः ।\nपरानभिमुखं यान्तं रथावास्थाय दंशितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will go after you, and so will Kritavarman of the Satvatas, both of us armored and mounted on our chariot, as you advance on the enemy."}},{"n":4,"text":"आवाभ्यां सहितः शत्रूञ्श्वोऽसि हन्ता समागमे ।\nविक्रम्य रथिनां श्रेष्ठ पाञ्चालान्सपदानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With us beside you, tomorrow you will kill the enemy in the clash, striking down the Panchalas with their followers, best of charioteers."}},{"n":5,"text":"शक्तस्त्वमसि विक्रान्तुं विश्रमस्व निशामिमाम् ।\nचिरं ते जाग्रतस्तात स्वप तावन्निशामिमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You are able to show your valor; rest this night. You have been awake a long time, dear one; sleep now for this night."}},{"n":6,"text":"विश्रान्तश्च विनिद्रश्च स्वस्थचित्तश्च मानद ।\nसमेत्य समरे शत्रून्वधिष्यसि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rested, refreshed by sleep and calm in mind, giver of honor, you will meet the enemy in battle and slay them, without doubt."}},{"n":7,"text":"न हि त्वा रथिनां श्रेष्ठ प्रगृहीतवरायुधम् ।\nजेतुमुत्सहते कश्चिदपि देवेषु पावकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of charioteers, with your fine weapon in hand, no one could dare to defeat you, not even a son of fire among the gods."}},{"n":8,"text":"कृपेण सहितं यान्तं युक्तं च कृतवर्मणा ।\nको द्रौणिं युधि संरब्धं योधयेदपि देवराट् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With Kripa beside him and Kritavarman attending, who could fight the son of Drona when he is roused to fury, even the king of the gods?"}},{"n":9,"text":"ते वयं परिविश्रान्ता विनिद्रा विगतज्वराः ।\nप्रभातायां रजन्यां वै निहनिष्याम शात्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, rested, with sleep behind us and our fever gone, we will kill the enemy when night turns to dawn."}},{"n":10,"text":"तव ह्यस्त्राणि दिव्यानि मम चैव न संशयः ।\nसात्वतोऽपि महेष्वासो नित्यं युद्धेषु कोविदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You have divine weapons, and so do I, no doubt; and the Satvata, a great archer, is ever skilled in battles."}},{"n":11,"text":"ते वयं सहितास्तात सर्वाञ्शत्रून्समागतान् ।\nप्रसह्य समरे हत्वा प्रीतिं प्राप्स्याम पुष्कलाम् ।\nविश्रमस्व त्वमव्यग्रः स्वप चेमां निशां सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together, dear one, we will overpower all the enemies who come against us and kill them in battle, and gain great joy. Rest without anxiety and sleep this night in comfort."}},{"n":12,"text":"अहं च कृतवर्मा च प्रयान्तं त्वां नरोत्तम ।\nअनुयास्याव सहितौ धन्विनौ परतापिनौ ।\nरथिनं त्वरया यान्तं रथावास्थाय दंशितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of men, Kritavarman and I, both archers who torment the foe, will follow you together as you go, armored and mounted on a chariot, when you hurry off on yours."}},{"n":13,"text":"स गत्वा शिबिरं तेषां नाम विश्राव्य चाहवे ।\nततः कर्तासि शत्रूणां युध्यतां कदनं महत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Going to their camp, announce your name in battle, and then you will work great slaughter among the enemy who fight."}},{"n":14,"text":"कृत्वा च कदनं तेषां प्रभाते विमलेऽहनि ।\nविहरस्व यथा शक्रः सूदयित्वा महासुरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having wrought that slaughter, at dawn on a clear day, make merry as Indra did after killing the mighty asuras."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वं हि शक्तो रणे जेतुं पाञ्चालानां वरूथिनीम् ।\nदैत्यसेनामिव क्रुद्धः सर्वदानवसूदनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For you are able to defeat the Panchala host in battle, like the slayer of all the danavas in wrath against the army of the daityas."}},{"n":16,"text":"मया त्वां सहितं संख्ये गुप्तं च कृतवर्मणा ।\nन सहेत विभुः साक्षाद्वज्रपाणिरपि स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With me beside you in the fight and Kritavarman guarding you, not even the mighty wielder of the thunderbolt himself could withstand you."}},{"n":17,"text":"न चाहं समरे तात कृतवर्मा तथैव च ।\nअनिर्जित्य रणे पाण्डून्व्यपयास्याव कर्हिचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And neither I, dear one, nor Kritavarman will ever turn back in battle without conquering the Pandavas."}},{"n":18,"text":"हत्वा च समरे क्षुद्रान्पाञ्चालान्पाण्डुभिः सह ।\nनिवर्तिष्यामहे सर्वे हता वा स्वर्गगा वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed the petty Panchalas together with the Pandavas, we shall come back, or else, slain, go to heaven."}},{"n":19,"text":"सर्वोपायैः सहायास्ते प्रभाते वयमेव हि ।\nसत्यमेतन्महाबाहो प्रब्रवीमि तवानघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"At dawn we shall indeed be your helpers by every means; this I tell you truly, mighty-armed, blameless one."}},{"n":20,"text":"एवमुक्तस्ततो द्रौणिर्मातुलेन हितं वचः ।\nअब्रवीन्मातुलं राजन्क्रोधादुद्वृत्य लोचने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by his maternal uncle with these salutary words, the son of Drona, O king, rolled his eyes in anger and answered his uncle."}},{"n":21,"text":"आतुरस्य कुतो निद्रा नरस्यामर्षितस्य च ।\nअर्थांश्चिन्तयतश्चापि कामयानस्य वा पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can a man who is in pain and resentful, who is thinking about his aims or who yearns for something, find sleep?"}},{"n":22,"text":"तदिदं समनुप्राप्तं पश्य मेऽद्य चतुष्टयम् ।\nयस्य भागश्चतुर्थो मे स्वप्नमह्नाय नाशयेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"See how this fourfold affliction has come to me today; any one share of it would drive away sleep at once."}},{"n":23,"text":"किं नाम दुःखं लोकेऽस्मिन्पितुर्वधमनुस्मरन् ।\nहृदयं निर्दहन्मेऽद्य रात्र्यहानि न शाम्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"What sorrow in this world compares, when I keep recalling my father's killing? It burns my heart and does not ease by night or day."}},{"n":24,"text":"यथा च निहतः पापैः पिता मम विशेषतः ।\nप्रत्यक्षमपि ते सर्वं तन्मे मर्माणि कृन्तति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And how my father was killed by sinners, especially, as I saw it all before my eyes, cuts my vitals."}},{"n":25,"text":"कथं हि मादृशो लोके मुहूर्तमपि जीवति ।\nद्रोणो हतेति यद्वाचः पाञ्चालानां शृणोम्यहम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can anyone like me live even a moment, when I hear the Panchalas shout, \"Drona is slain!\""}},{"n":26,"text":"दृष्टद्युम्नमहत्वाजौ नाहं जीवितुमुत्सहे ।\nस मे पितृवधाद्वध्यः पाञ्चाला ये च संगताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Without killing Dhrishtadyumna in battle I cannot bear to live; for killing my father, he must die, and the Panchalas gathered with him."}},{"n":27,"text":"विलापो भग्नसक्थस्य यस्तु राज्ञो मया श्रुतः ।\nस पुनर्हृदयं कस्य क्रूरस्यापि न निर्दहेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the lament of the king with broken thighs that I heard would burn the heart even of a cruel man."}},{"n":28,"text":"कस्य ह्यकरुणस्यापि नेत्राभ्यामश्रु नाव्रजेत् ।\nनृपतेर्भग्नसक्थस्य श्रुत्वा तादृग्वचः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whose eyes, even of a pitiless person, would not fill with tears on hearing again such words from the king with shattered thighs?"}},{"n":29,"text":"यश्चायं मित्रपक्षो मे मयि जीवति निर्जितः ।\nशोकं मे वर्धयत्येष वारिवेग इवार्णवम् ।\nएकाग्रमनसो मेऽद्य कुतो निद्रा कुतः सुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And this circle of my friends that was beaten while I live only increases my sorrow, as a flood swells the ocean; with a mind fixed on one thing, how can I sleep today, how be at ease?"}},{"n":30,"text":"वासुदेवार्जुनाभ्यां हि तानहं परिरक्षितान् ।\nअविषह्यतमान्मन्ये महेन्द्रेणापि मातुल ॥","meaning":{"en":"I believe those men, protected by Vasudeva and Arjuna, cannot be withstood even by Mahendra, uncle."}},{"n":31,"text":"न चास्मि शक्यः संयन्तुमस्मात्कार्यात्कथंचन ।\nन तं पश्यामि लोकेऽस्मिन्यो मां कार्यान्निवर्तयेत् ।\nइति मे निश्चिता बुद्धिरेषा साधुमता च मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nor can I be restrained from this task in any way; I see no one in this world who could turn me back from it. This is my settled resolve, and I find it right."}},{"n":32,"text":"वार्त्तिकैः कथ्यमानस्तु मित्राणां मे पराभवः ।\nपाण्डवानां च विजयो हृदयं दहतीव मे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing messengers report the defeat of my friends and the victory of the Pandavas feels like a fire in my heart."}},{"n":33,"text":"अहं तु कदनं कृत्वा शत्रूणामद्य सौप्तिके ।\nततो विश्रमिता चैव स्वप्ता च विगतज्वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But after I have wrought slaughter on the enemy in tonight's sleeping attack, then I shall rest and sleep, my fever gone."}}]}]}